      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name}: just to bump this thread, there are a lot of parts of the world (India, South East Asia, China) in which trackers are either prohibitively expensive for the majority, or flat out not available. As a software dev, I know edge cases are a pain to support, but given the interface into the spatial data for trackers and controllers is essentially identical, this shouldn't be that big of a problem, especially when the consequences of not supporting it essentially cuts off half a continent (many of whom have spent money on your service) of people who've put time and effort getting what they can find to work in order to enjoy what you guys have made. I - and many others - eagerly await a fix.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
